# cpmtools disk format definitions for the images in this directory.
#
# Why this file exists.  cpmtools reads ./diskdefs if there is one and
# /etc/cpmtools/diskdefs (or the homebrew equivalent) otherwise - one or the
# other, never both - and the per-slice combo definitions are not in every
# distribution's copy.  Debian and Ubuntu's cpmtools 2.23 ships wbw_hd1k and
# NOT wbw_hd1k_0, which is the definition hd1k_combo.img needs, so on those
# machines both scripts here reported "r8.com is not on the image at all" for a
# file that is on it.  That is the same wrong-diskdef failure mode the two
# scripts warn about: cpmtools does not fail on a bad format name in a way the
# scripts could tell apart from a missing file.
#
# Because ./diskdefs REPLACES the system file rather than adding to it, this
# has to carry every definition the scripts use, not just the missing ones.
# Both scripts run cpmls/cpmcp/cpmrm with this directory as the working
# directory so that they pick it up wherever they are invoked from.
#
# wbw_hd1k is copied from the stock cpmtools file.  The slice definitions are
# the same geometry with an offset: a combo image is a 1 MB MBR prefix followed
# by whole 8 MB slices (docs/DISK_FORMATS.md).

# RomWBW 8 MB hard disk slice, 1024 directory entries.  A plain single-slice
# image - hd1k_infocom.img - is exactly this and nothing else.
diskdef wbw_hd1k
  seclen 512
  tracks 1024
  sectrk 16
  blocksize 4096
  maxdir 1024
  skew 0
  boottrk 2
  os 2.2
end

# Combo images: the same slice, past the 1 MB MBR prefix and then N whole
# slices.  offset is in bytes: 1048576 + 8388608 * slice.
diskdef wbw_hd1k_0
  seclen 512
  tracks 1024
  sectrk 16
  blocksize 4096
  maxdir 1024
  skew 0
  boottrk 2
  offset 1048576
  os 2.2
end

# Slices 1 and up are deliberately NOT defined here.  The geometry is the same
# with offset = 1048576 + 8388608 * slice, but on hd1k_combo.img every one of
# them answers "cannot read superblock (Bad parameter)" - checked for slices 1,
# 2 and 3, in all four of cpmtools' offset units - so whatever those slices
# hold, it is not a directory these parameters describe.  Nothing in this
# repository reads them.  Add one when there is an image to check it against;
# an unverified definition here would be exactly the silently-wrong diskdef
# both scripts exist to warn about.
